---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---

<Legal
  title="Cookie policy"
  metaTitle="Cookie policy | Espoir Care"
  description="Which cookies the Espoir Care website uses, what Google Analytics sets if you accept, and how to change your choice at any time."
  path="/cookie-policy/"
  lead="What we store in your browser and how to change your choice."
  updated="29 October 2026"
>
  <h2>What cookies are</h2>
  <p>Cookies are small files a website saves in your browser. Some are needed for a site to work. Others help the owner understand how the site is used.</p>

  <h2>What we use</h2>
  <h3>Your cookie choice</h3>
  <p>
    When you choose "Accept analytics" or "Decline", we remember your choice in your browser's local storage under the name <code>espoir-consent</code>.
    It is not a cookie and it is never sent to us. It just stops the cookie banner from showing on every page.
  </p>

  <h3>Google Analytics (only if you accept)</h3>
  <p>
    If you choose "Accept analytics", we load Google Analytics 4. It tells us which pages people visit, how they found the site and what kind of device
    they use, so we can make the site easier to use. Until you accept, Google Analytics does not load at all and no analytics cookies are set.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <caption class="visually-hidden">Cookies set by Google Analytics</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Cookie</th>
          <th scope="col">What it does</th>
          <th scope="col">How long it lasts</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>_ga</code></td>
          <td>Tells one visitor apart from another</td>
          <td>2 years</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>_ga_</code> followed by an ID</td>
          <td>Keeps track of your current visit</td>
          <td>2 years</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    We use Google Consent Mode with everything turned off by default. Even if you accept analytics, advertising features stay off. Google's own privacy
    policy explains how Google handles this data:
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.
  </p>

  <h3>What we do not use</h3>
  <p>We do not use advertising cookies, tracking pixels, social media plugins or embedded maps.</p>

  <h3>Forms, fonts and links</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Our enquiry and contact forms do not set cookies. When you send a form, what you type goes to our form service, Web3Forms, which passes it on to
      us by email. Our <a href={url('/privacy-policy/')}>privacy policy</a> explains more.
    </li>
    <li>Our fonts are stored on our own website, so loading a page does not contact Google Fonts or any other font service.</li>
    <li>
      Links to Facebook, Instagram, LinkedIn and Google Maps are plain links. Nothing from those sites loads until you click one, and then their own
      cookie policies apply.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="cookie-settings">Changing your choice</h2>
  <p>You can change your mind at any time. Use the "Cookie settings" link at the bottom of every page, or this button:</p>
  <p class="js-only"><button type="button" class="btn btn--secondary" data-cookie-settings>Change cookie settings</button></p>
  <noscript>
    <p>JavaScript is turned off in your browser, so Google Analytics cannot load and no analytics cookies are set.</p>
  </noscript>
  <p>
    If you decline after accepting, we remove the Google Analytics cookies we can reach. You can also clear cookies in your browser settings, or install
    Google's <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">opt-out browser add-on</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>More information</h2>
  <p>Our <a href={url('/privacy-policy/')}>privacy policy</a> explains how we handle personal information.</p>
</Legal>

<style>
  .js-only {
    display: none;
  }
  :global(.js) .js-only {
    display: block;
  }
</style>
